\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{49fff61}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The project's metric is warm wall clock, and for it a process has to check the same export more than once. With \code{\verb~|passes=N~}, 1 to 1000, pass 1 is the run itself and gives the verdict and the exit status. Passes 2 to N check every definition, theorem, axiom and opaque constant again over the same store with new engines, sessions, scheduler and board, and are made only when pass 1 accepted. Each pass prints one line with its verdict, wall and CPU time. On the prelude export with the machine and 4 workers on the JVM launcher the check phase takes 0.790, 0.238 and 0.220 s in passes 1, 2 and 3. A later pass has no load and no environment pass. Published with 101 tests, 98 run green and 3 opt-in.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-driver/README.md}. Commit \commit{49fff61}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE).}
